<BODY>&nbsp;</TD>
    <td align="left" vAlign="top">&nbsp;
		<table align="left" border="0" cellPadding="1" cellSpacing="1" width="100%">
        
			<tr>
				<td style="WIDTH: 15px" width="15"></td>
				<td align="left" class="TextMain">
					<center><h2> Guild Rules And Conduct</h2></center>
      <P>
					The following rules of conduct and guidelines have been set forth as to make our playing
					time more enjoyable and fruitful, and not as a means to take away
					 from the total gaming
					experience.<br>
					<br>
					1) Conduct:<br>
					<br>
					With regard to conduct and attitudes, we encourage people to have fun, laugh and enjoy
					each other’s company. But this does not mean to participate in
					 offensive behavior that
					may be degrading to other members or even yourself. Please try to police your own actions
					or they may be reviewed for guild disciplinary
					 actions by our review board.<br>
					<br>
					Some of the more serious offenses, which are viewed with disdain, are, kill stealing,
					deliberate deception and any attempt to defraud guild members as
					 well as other players.
					Our guild members should adhere to the General Guidelines as indicated by Verant.
					Lying, undermining other members, begging or
					 leaving your wiped out group without
					offering to help are examples of conduct we wish not have associated with At Deaths
					Door. When in doubt about a conduct
					 issue, contact a guild officer for advice - "Ignorance"
					is not a viable excuse.<br>
					<br>
					Use common sense when dealing with problems with guildmates and others. Try to
					solve any problems that you may encounter on your own at first. If you
					 cannot, then please
					get an officer involved before making snap decisions.<br>
					<br>
					Its every guild members duty to act as a guild custodian and police not only your own,
					but others actions of guild members. Please be discreet when
					 handling these situations
					and not openly berate members in an open guild chat forum unless no other recourse
					is available.<br>
					<br>
					2) Guild Chat:<br>
					<br>
					This guild has open enrollment to many diverse age groups, so we as guild members
					have an obligation to keep chat relatively free of offensive language
					 and any connotations
					toward sexual or racial content. Please respect each other and use discretion as appropriate.
					We strive to be as helpful as possible
					 with quests, advice, pricing and other game topics.
					Guild Chat should be a non-discriminatory harassment free environment.<br>
					<br>
					3) Interaction:<br>
					<br>
					Guild members should strive to be as helpful when the time merits it. The reputation
					of all us individuals will have a big impact of how others view us as a
					 guild. Be courteous
					and friendly.<br>
					<br>
					4) Power Leveling:<br>
					<br>
					We believe that a player who earns his or her way through this world will be a much stronger
					asset to the guild. Power leveling a “Primary Character” is not
					 recommended. If you
					are not of a group level to obtain an item, then it is not meant for you.<br>
					<br>
					If you do “power level” then we ask you to use discretion and keep it out of guild chat. Players
					should “never” expect help with power leveling or
					 twinking.<br>
					<br>
					<br>
					5) Guild Based items and Skills:<br>
					<br>
					We request (not require) that guild members with trade skills offer their assistance
					to guildmates at close to cost with regards to any items which<br>
					need to be purchased to make a particular item.<br>
					<br>
					If an item is given to you by another guildmate, and you don’t require its use anymore,
					then we recommend that you pass it on to another guildmate of
					 appropriate level when
					applicable.<br>
					<br>
					<br>
					6) Guild Invites :<br>
					<br>
					a) Currently, the minimum level for guild invite is of the 50th season unless authorized
					by the guild leader. It is the responsibility of our officers to
					 strictly adhere and enforce
					this rule.<br>
					<br>b) 
					All new invites will go through a&nbsp;6 week&nbsp;trial period to assess that persons conduct and playing habits. They will be known
					as 'Recruits' during this stage.&nbsp; While in this trial period,
					 the&nbsp;'Recruit' is still subject to ADD
					rules regarding dismissals. (see following section on guild dismissals)<br>
					<br>
					c) All new invites are the ultimate responsibility of the person who invited them during
					their initial trial stage. After the trial stage, any
					 disciplinary action, which may need
					to take place, will be subject to ADD dismissal policy.<br>
					<br>
					d) UPON INITIAL INVITATION the officer must first make the new invite aware of
					the ADD rule section on our website. The new member or inviting officer
					 must place
					the following information in the “Trial Membership Section” of the guildsite:<br>
					1: Name of player.<br>
					2: Level and Class<br>
					3: Race in Game<br>
					4: Date of Invite<br>
					5: Any general comments<br>
					<br>
					e) An appeal to the guild leader by the inviting officer and not the invitee to skip the trial
					Membership period if that person is known and can be vouched
					 for by the inviting officer.		<br></P>
					<P>f) During the first six week period, the Recruit will not receive any 
					help for quests items.&nbsp; After this time, they will receive the full 
					support of their guild on their quests.&nbsp; Recruits will be required to 
					attend at least two raids during their six week trial.
					<br>
					<br>
					7) Dismissals:<br>
					<br>
					A) Once a month an exploratory panel of officers will meet to discuss and devise ways
					to minimize any breaches of guild or game protocol.<br>
					<br>
					B) Offenses to guild protocol will be handled in such a manner that the offending player
					will receive the “OBLIGATORY” two- (2) verbal warnings via
					 private tells.<br>
					<br>
					C) It is not the sole responsibility of any officer to dismiss any one player without that
					person having his or her proverbial day in court (see line D).
					 This dismissal ruling can
					be null and void if the offense is serious enough that the player is causing a great disruption
					to guild harmony and continuity.
					 Thusly, the dismissed individual can petition the guild
					leader for re-admittance. Upon re-admittance the offending person will provide a guild
					apology in
					 guild chat for his actions. In essence taking responsibility for ones actions
					will only strengthen ones character and guild status.<br>
					<br>
					D) Dismissals are handled in such a manner only when all avenues of action are exhausted.
					Guild dismissal is not an arbitrary action but one that should
					 be taken into great consideration.
					We as guild members have a mission to further educate our fellow guildmates on conduct
					becoming an ADD member. Unless
					 all avenues of discipline have been exhausted or
					the offense is of an extremely serious nature (see conduct section), then dismissal
					is warranted only by
					 consensus of “Three” guild officers. The dismissing officer upon
					taking this course of action must notify the player of his offense and what course of action
					he
					 can take to get re-admitted to the guild. Due to the size of our guild, it has recently
					become necessary to enact these rules of dismissal<br>
					<br>
					E) Upon dismissal, any player may then petition the guild leader for re-admittance to
					the guild. But first the guild leader must poll the officers
					 involved in the dismissal and
					a ruling will be considered.<br></P>
				</td>
